  {
    "id": "5269ccec8fbe33c694dc",
    "source": "Two choices decide who reads a line aloud. **The narrator's voice and pace** read the story, and every speaker who has no voice of their own. **Character voices** belong to one speaker each. With *Each speaker gets a voice*, everyone who speaks (an innkeeper, a monster, a companion) is given one of this server's voices the first time they talk and keeps it from then on. With *The narrator reads them*, nobody is given one automatically, and any voice you do give a character still plays. Either way, a voice can be given or changed per character once the campaign has people in it: {0}. Each player can also choose the voice their own character speaks in there. This is the table's spoken narration. Live voice chat between players is a separate setting.",
    "sourceHash": "5269ccec8fbe33c694dc005539181029854a45967184c0e9fa690dd82df86fac",
